#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110351 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/id #uuid "30974188-c734-5e99-a9ae-81d1a53b9105" :question/math-academy-id "e-14854" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched below.\n\n![](images/e5/e5393f15ff154f1f4cc310791790db0fe0ad0d9faa076d10f3f6ec7b481de086.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-3+2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110352 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/id #uuid "00575d99-28e6-59b7-b416-765808916fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14857" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x-1)(x-5).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=-(x-1)(x-5),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=1$ and $x_2=5.$\n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2} = \\dfrac{1+5}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110353 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/id #uuid "405e0230-69cb-5679-bec0-13a69c722934" :question/math-academy-id "e-14860" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2)$ is $x=6.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6,$ we will set our result equal to $6.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=k$ and $x_2=-2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k-2}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k-2}{2} & =6 \\\\ k-2 & =12 \\\\ k & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110373 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/id #uuid "04877936-271e-5fcb-a1ea-aa39c52482b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-19740" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $4$ | $12$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $9$ | $25$ | $9$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y = f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=4$ and $x=20$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(4) = f(20) = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=4$ and $x=20.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabolas vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{4+20}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e9f3df9-da61-5f4a-b3ab-8a1a1cda444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540607} {:answer/id #uuid "62de6123-6a95-5dae-88e9-843c5a0c968d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540695} {:answer/id #uuid "cac0d315-ce7f-5d80-9e6a-46b1ae01e841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540866} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0cfaa1-d45c-5039-a04f-63b0fdededc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540902} {:answer/id #uuid "e784cab5-862c-5407-ae59-9868332a3944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e9f3df9-da61-5f4a-b3ab-8a1a1cda444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540607} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba3ac59-9466-58f5-9b5b-efe7c90f5528" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "094a6192-1567-5375-9e5c-b0ab7210d2c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-106137" :question/problem "![](images/e1/e1fdcc8a8ed9dd9936ade0b088a672eadea1ca9ae7b12de7ce1b1dead2c3014a.png)\n\nFind the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=-4$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{(-4)+2}{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68e7c17d-7e12-5d3e-afd5-011a186ee008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563188} {:answer/id #uuid "91189e9e-756c-5779-950e-f011041ff2b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563269} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f22b06-7510-59cb-af7d-fe434eed0c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563316} {:answer/id #uuid "db18c12c-2087-5905-9c74-6abb04f1a1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563425} {:answer/id #uuid "df1b1902-78e7-5bd8-b4d4-f1c766ecff16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91189e9e-756c-5779-950e-f011041ff2b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563269} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ffa1566-4612-5862-8fdf-ac5382f57169" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a1b4ade-6b6f-5b17-86f4-ce0cd6af2275" :question/math-academy-id "q-106153" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x+1)(x+5).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(x+1)(x+5),$ we can tell that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=-5.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)+(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39ae4953-ea9c-5671-8840-4018a5578e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563074} {:answer/id #uuid "6669511f-d4ef-5505-b173-a7475fbc1511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563183} {:answer/id #uuid "9e91fbe8-a391-5c1a-b5f5-c38ffbd44c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563301} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563349} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f335a4-a3ee-545c-8578-89d25b02d49d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563349} :answer-field/id #uuid "70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12" :question/math-academy-id "q-106169" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of $y=(x-2k)(x+3k)$ is $x=-2.$ The value of $k=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-2,$ we will set our result equal to $-2.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(x-2k)(x+3k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=2k$ and ${x}_{2}=-3k.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2k+(-3k)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-k}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-k}{2} & =-2 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ebf46c9-f938-50a8-9cc1-97df4784c6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ebf46c9-f938-50a8-9cc1-97df4784c6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563161} :answer-field/id #uuid "79bc61fa-11bd-5db1-aa6e-3d865e60342d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e6642fc-4b0f-571e-8c66-e87cc2512b11" :question/math-academy-id "q-220354" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bd46cb7a3139ccb19b7f65bab927ef8c56ba075520262649d6fa196cdab8cc81.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a parabola. The $x$-coordinates of $A$ and $B$ are $-\\frac{16}{5}$ and $\\frac{5}{2},$ respectively.  Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola.\n\nThe axis of symmetry is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We're given that the roots of the parabola are \n ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{16}{5}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{16}{5}+\\frac{5}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{32}{10}+\\frac{25}{10})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{10})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{7}{20}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47acc35f-5b61-5d14-8bcc-66ac1ea76bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47acc35f-5b61-5d14-8bcc-66ac1ea76bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540654} :answer-field/id #uuid "caf9ab22-db76-5d02-b2ce-c710382a7b35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f8c9da4-4b17-554e-b183-7584d639d444" :question/math-academy-id "q-223659" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b0ebd3a9a282fca4dc4302549c22efe674ada772eb00ed5e8aa0abbe275074b.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a parabola. The $x$-coordinates of $A$ and $B$ are $-\\frac{8}{3}$ and $\\frac{11}{5},$ respectively.  Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola.\n\nThe axis of symmetry is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We're given that the roots of the parabola are \n ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{11}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{11}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{40}{15}+\\frac{33}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{7}{30}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fb5a3b2-6779-5f18-aee9-35c71d01843c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fb5a3b2-6779-5f18-aee9-35c71d01843c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555296} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff2d3b83-418c-57aa-abbd-ad23104f3a79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c9a4b7b-8e3b-5aa3-8825-873abec27dfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-223666" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x-1)(x-9)$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(x-1)(x-9),$ we can tell that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=9.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563299} :answer-field/id #uuid "b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4cf4852d-d3c2-5b9a-829d-615cf17e0f68" :question/math-academy-id "q-223668" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x+6)(x-4)$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=-(x+6)(x-4),$ we can tell that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-6$ and ${x}_{2}=4.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6+4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563458} :answer-field/id #uuid "e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563634}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-223686" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(2x+3)(x-k)$ is $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{5}{4},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{5}{4}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(2x+3)(x-k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=k.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2}+k)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2k}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2k-3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2k-3}{4} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ 2k-3 & =5 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563182} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fc6a2b7-5d2f-5c82-ae12-de24bf2f6659" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8660b4e2-d758-5150-9ae4-48bf3487cb6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-223695" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x+5k)(3x-4k)$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{8}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{8},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{1}{8}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=-(x+5k)(3x-4k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-5k$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{4k}{3}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-5k+\\frac{4k}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-\\frac{11k}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11k}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{8}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11k}{6} & =-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ -11k & =-\\frac{6}{8} \\\\ -11k & =-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ k & =\\frac{3}{44}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14015542-fee2-5fec-96da-f18d0ae334d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562985} {:answer/id #uuid "3f931ccf-9536-5f59-b52c-f7140f39f8f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563090} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0dd0eb-fb35-581b-aab9-f1d675a126de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563125} {:answer/id #uuid "c46a3c63-7ce2-5171-80e2-c72b810d3bbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563374} {:answer/id #uuid "e4bcb35f-829f-5234-a877-ca4c41be4fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14015542-fee2-5fec-96da-f18d0ae334d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562985} :answer-field/id #uuid "1123def6-8dc6-58e4-8f1b-899f255bbcc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8e7577e-52b0-551a-a683-aebcdeb0ba63" :question/math-academy-id "q-30510" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6ecca5e6b96cd7e0de0510abf26b3fe80c6f33322460b9bf4448f4b9c3eb8442.png)\n\nFind the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{(-1)+2}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563395} :answer-field/id #uuid "7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563574}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-311909" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $8$ | $10$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $18$ | $12$ | $12$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=10$ and $x=16$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(10)=f(16)=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=10$ and $x=16.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabola's vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{10+16}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{2} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563659 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563365} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-311952" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $-4$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $0$ | $-12$ | $0$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=-4\\,\\text{and}\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{-4+3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562963} :answer-field/id #uuid "97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27" :question/math-academy-id "q-311955" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $2$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $0$ | $8$ | $0$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. The parabola opens downward. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=2\\,\\text{and}\\,x=8.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{2+8}{2} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563428} :answer-field/id #uuid "19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-311956" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $-9$ | $-6$ | $-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $-10$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. The parabola opens downward. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=-6\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-3.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{-6+(-3)}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{47}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563084} :answer-field/id #uuid "20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77" :question/math-academy-id "q-311977" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $22$ | $25$ | $29$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $7$ | $7$ | $1$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=22$ and $x=25$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(22)=f(25)=7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=22$ and $x=25.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabola's vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{22+25}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{47}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15eb53f7-fe67-57d6-a2b0-7d5a7be0aef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562991} {:answer/id #uuid "383662d8-7c53-56e6-b7ee-0d5555963c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563071} {:answer/id #uuid "a718f457-e6e2-5d83-99f8-1f151c1c909b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563323} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d96b22-da80-52f9-b2f6-8c6bc1bb1aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563419} {:answer/id #uuid "efc78a1d-c863-5959-83d0-6a25a98b5920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7d96b22-da80-52f9-b2f6-8c6bc1bb1aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563419} :answer-field/id #uuid "d992778b-a9e3-5c64-9ebe-4a79b06c6533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9694bfd-2888-58c6-a0ef-19d3c4d9b6a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-84895" :question/problem "![](images/ce/ce468433e58a99da31fb305428ff478ddb4c91ec6fa260ab1a951979e83ec63c.png)\n\nFind the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=-4$ and ${x}_{2}=3.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{(-4)+3}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562986} {:answer/id #uuid "169d9c2b-ed8e-5399-9665-91d1666641d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562994} {:answer/id #uuid "29e329a9-3422-59f4-82ad-91d038159e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563039} {:answer/id #uuid "404a6d55-06c7-5863-9890-05c5ef448ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563093} {:answer/id #uuid "80b7f6d3-2e98-5ccb-856a-d66a6512df21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562986} :answer-field/id #uuid "329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-84902" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(6x-1)(3x+1).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(6x-1)(3x+1),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{6}$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{2}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{12}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05ed7714-762b-563c-aa6e-395fc6bb299a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562950} {:answer/id #uuid "12226c0d-85bd-508b-82d8-13bf97d8f83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562981} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd14c1c-2112-52ab-bcdc-5d7b174123b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563079} {:answer/id #uuid "55af48ee-55a1-5c40-847d-5742b568cea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563140} {:answer/id #uuid "f8844c5c-08d4-51a1-8c11-9ac8c49c3885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05ed7714-762b-563c-aa6e-395fc6bb299a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562950} :answer-field/id #uuid "707a53ec-3f89-531c-a47b-914f51a9c97c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da0e0865-56b2-565d-ac33-deaee1268cf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-84903" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(7-5x)(x+1).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(7-5x)(x+1),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{7}{5}$ and ${x}_{2}=-1.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{5}-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{5}-\\frac{5}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563697 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7dd35c-387e-5c8f-8d52-8df49f54ba91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563008} {:answer/id #uuid "2231137b-d7d1-5097-a668-5b88fce4d605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563022} {:answer/id #uuid "8240c150-e4cb-507a-8888-b6ef07b60c64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563234} {:answer/id #uuid "96e7ced7-ae8e-524c-9f9a-e5c32bd8d7a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563283} {:answer/id #uuid "f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563488} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-84906" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(3x+4)(6x-k)$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ The value of $k=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{3},$ we will set our result equal to $-\\frac{1}{3}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=-(3x+4)(6x-k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{k}{6}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{k}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{6}+\\frac{k}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k-8}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k-8}{12} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ k-8 & =-4 \\\\ k & =-4+8 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563646 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193c9dde-df02-57fb-9a38-2e3ada1317a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563003} {:answer/id #uuid "45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563100} {:answer/id #uuid "7f53d534-d2c5-55c9-bc0b-0b43335f20b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563225} {:answer/id #uuid "a475de87-e762-598f-af2f-5e440020dd19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563317} {:answer/id #uuid "ff07e237-c85a-5da5-b75b-ecc1a90cc0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563100} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/math-academy-id "q-84911" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of $y=\\frac{1}{3}(k-x)(5x+3k)$ is $x=\\frac{1}{10}.$ The value of $k=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{10},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{1}{10}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=\\frac{1}{3}(k-x)(5x+3k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=k$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{3k}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k-\\frac{3k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{5k}{5}-\\frac{3k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{10}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{5} & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
